WEBVTT

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:11.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday the sixth of March. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:15.449
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, got you. Bit tinny, but that's probably this headset.</v>

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:22.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we start— the football last night. Honestly, ninety minutes I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:27.239
<v Callum Reid>You say that every Friday. Still watch it, though.</v>

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:37.149
<v Sarah Okafor>And the broken coffee machine in the canteen isn't helping. That's a moan, by the way, not another job for this meeting.</v>

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:45.740
<v Aisha Begum>Try the heating in the portakabin. I'm sat here in my coat. Also just moaning, before anyone puts my name against anything.</v>

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.149
<v Tomasz Nowak>Very efficient meeting so far. Football, coffee, being cold.</v>

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, yeah, factory stuff. Anything already closed out first?</v>

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.619
<v Hannah Price>I tested the 11kV board yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done.</v>

00:01:01.159 --> 00:01:06.409
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, so that's a completed item, not another test we're trying to fit in today?</v>

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.439
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. Just giving you the result.</v>

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:15.909
<v Sarah Okafor>And I finished the repair on the CT1 last night. That's closed as well.</v>

00:01:17.099 --> 00:01:20.950
<v Marcus Hale>Good. Two things off rather than six things on, for once.</v>

00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:29.049
<v Aisha Begum>Just an observation from nights: noticed the palletizer was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:30.349 --> 00:01:33.150
<v Callum Reid>Settled before the end of nights, you mean?</v>

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:39.590
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah. Not raising any work off that, just passing on what happened.</v>

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:47.739
<v Tomasz Nowak>And my existing blocker hasn't changed. I can't get to the line three until production gives us a window.</v>

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:54.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Still blocked, then; that's not a fresh instruction to go in today.</v>

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:04.200
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the MV01 by Wednesday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.949
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the MV01 by Wednesday. Understood on doing that first.</v>

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Han. That's agreed.</v>

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:21.830
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 this morning. Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:27.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tom. Guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1, this morning, normal priority.</v>

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep. That's the one I'm taking.</v>

00:02:31.979 --> 00:02:35.479
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, talked over the end of that. Heard you now.</v>

00:02:37.419 --> 00:02:46.520
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, I'll schedule downtime for the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit with production by Thursday. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—I've got that.</v>

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:52.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Cal. By Thursday for getting the downtime scheduled, agreed.</v>

00:02:54.479 --> 00:02:59.030
<v Callum Reid>Exactly, that's the scheduling bit. Not saying all the work happens on Thursday.</v>

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:10.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate from that, Callum, can you swap the filter on the line one HPU by 11am? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:17.759
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll swap the filter on the line one HPU by 11am. That gets the urgent slot.</v>

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.389
<v Aisha Begum>Right, I nearly bundled those together in my head. Two separate commitments, then.</v>

00:03:25.289 --> 00:03:31.240
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Filter by 11am; scheduling the downtime by Thursday. Not waiting for Thursday to do the filter.</v>

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:36.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. The filter and the MV01 sign-off are the production-holding ones, not routine items.</v>

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.650
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I've got the MV01 sign-off first on mine, by Wednesday.</v>

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:49.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you send the shift handover report round as well, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:55.979
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round whenever I get a chance. Got it.</v>

00:03:57.319 --> 00:03:59.069
<v Marcus Hale>The glamorous side of production.</v>

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:01.919
<v Callum Reid>Living the dream. Mostly in a spreadsheet.</v>

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.930
<v Hannah Price>And I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next Tuesday. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Forklift Fleet pre-use checks next Tuesday, normal priority, agreed.</v>

00:04:16.139 --> 00:04:17.889
<v Hannah Price>Yep, next Tuesday for mine.</v>

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:22.329
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, was that Tuesday or Thursday? Teams swallowed the middle.</v>

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.629
<v Hannah Price>Tuesday. The Forklift Fleet pre-use checks are next Tuesday.</v>

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:38.769
<v Marcus Hale>There's still the permit gap, though. Someone needs to sort the permit to work and isolation for the line 3 at half two. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:40.259 --> 00:04:47.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Who can take that? At half two is the timing, but sorting that safety-critical gap needs attention straight away.</v>

00:04:48.839 --> 00:04:55.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take it. Like I said, can't get to the line three until production gives us a window.</v>

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:03.430
<v Priya Raman>I'm not taking ownership of that either. Don't put it against me because I'm on the call.</v>

00:05:04.939 --> 00:05:07.740
<v Callum Reid>No offer from me on that one, sorry.</v>

00:05:09.149 --> 00:05:11.949
<v Aisha Begum>So we haven't actually got anyone accepting it?</v>

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.550
<v Marcus Hale>No. I'm flagging the gap, not volunteering for the permit or the isolation.</v>

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:29.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Hearing no taker. The permit to work and isolation for the line 3 at half two is still unowned. That one's safety critical, straight away—not something we're calling covered.</v>

00:05:29.689 --> 00:05:34.589
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, don't want a mention in a stand-up being mistaken for a signed permit.</v>

00:05:35.939 --> 00:05:38.740
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Still a gap, not an agreed isolation.</v>

00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:43.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Nobody's accepted that one, and this conversation isn't authorisation to proceed.</v>

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:50.100
<v Priya Raman>Right. That's clear now. Bit of a difference between being on the list and being sorted.</v>

00:05:52.220 --> 00:06:07.620
<v Callum Reid>Mine are clear: filter on the line one HPU by 11am, first because it's holding production up. Schedule downtime for the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit with production by Thursday—not an emergency, but don't let it slip. Handover report whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:16.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 this morning, normal priority. The line three access is still blocked, separate thing.</v>

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:28.250
<v Hannah Price>I've got the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the MV01 by Wednesday, first because it's holding production up. And the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next Tuesday, normal priority.</v>

00:06:29.259 --> 00:06:35.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Those commitments are agreed; the line 3 permit and isolation remains unowned. That's the position, no pretending otherwise.</v>

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:37.870
<v Marcus Hale>Yep. Heard.</v>

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:47.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks all. And no, this call has not magically fixed the coffee machine either. See you on the floor.</v>
